            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$216$",
              "worked": "Each die has six possible results, so the number of ordered outcomes is $6\\times6\\times6=216$.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 10,
            "responseSpace": "scaffold"
          },
          {
            "id": "p27-challenge-q3-a-ii",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "ii",
            "prompt": "",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$\\frac{125}{216}$",
              "worked": "Each die has five results other than six, giving $5^3=125$ favourable outcomes.\n\n$$P(\\text{no sixes})=\\frac{5^3}{6^3}=\\frac{125}{216}.$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 19,
            "responseSpace": "scaffold"
          },
          {
            "id": "p27-challenge-q3-a-iii",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "iii",
            "prompt": "",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$\\frac{91}{216}$",
              "worked": "The complement of obtaining at least one six is obtaining no sixes.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{at least one six})&=1-\\frac{125}{216}\\\\P(\\text{at least one six})&=\\frac{91}{216}.\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 19,
            "responseSpace": "scaffold"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p27-challenge-q3-b",
