            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$6^n$",
              "worked": "There are six choices at each of $n$ stages, so the number of ordered outcomes is $6^n$.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 10,
            "responseSpace": "scaffold"
          },
          {
            "id": "p27-challenge-q3-c-ii",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "ii",
            "prompt": "",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$\\left(\\frac56\\right)^n$\n\nCount five non-six choices for each die out of six possible choices.",
              "worked": "There are $5^n$ outcomes containing no sixes and $6^n$ equally likely outcomes in total.\n\n$$P(\\text{no sixes})=\\frac{5^n}{6^n}=\\left(\\frac56\\right)^n.$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 19,
            "responseSpace": "scaffold"
          },
          {
            "id": "p27-challenge-q3-c-iii",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "iii",
            "prompt": "",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$1-\\left(\\frac56\\right)^n$\n\nSubtract the probability of no sixes from 1.",
              "worked": "The events ‘no sixes’ and ‘at least one six’ are complementary.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{at least one six})&=1-P(\\text{no sixes})\\\\P(\\text{at least one six})&=1-\\left(\\frac56\\right)^n.\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 19,
            "responseSpace": "scaffold"
          }
        ]
